# QR-360° viewer sync (QR-East_Industrial_Database)

## Two products, one semver

| Product | Badge | Where |
|---------|-------|--------|
| **QR360** | `QR360-vX.Y.Z` | Standalone Inspections (file / `:8788` / workers.dev) |
| **Map360** | `Map360-vX.Y.Z` | Map app iframe (`public/insp360/viewer.html`) |

Same patch numbers (`1.2.9`). Different **prefix** so you can tell which viewer you are in. Embed mode always shows **Map360**.

## Source of truth

`C:\Users\Robert\Projects\QR-360°-Inspections\QR-360°-Inspections`

New builds are named like `QR-360°_viewer_v1.2.9.html` (stamped **QR360** in source).

Viewer patch numbers stop at **99**, then the middle number increases (`v1.1.99` → `v1.2.0`). Same rule as the map app topbar.

## Linked locations

| Purpose | Path | Badge |
|---------|------|-------|
| Versioned archive | `qr360-viewer/QR-360°_viewer_v*.html` | **Map360** (after sync) |
| Live iframe target | `public/insp360/viewer.html` | **Map360** |
| App URL builder | `src/lib/insp360Viewer.ts` → `insp360/viewer.html` | — |

The main program must keep using **`insp360/viewer.html`** (stable). Never point the iframe at a versioned filename.

**Two copies of the map app:** run sync in **both** when shipping:

1. `C:\Users\Robert\Projects\QR-East_Industrial_Database` (local + GitHub source of truth)
2. `C:\Users\Robert\Projects\QR-East_Industrial_Database-Cloudflare` (quadreal Pages working mirror)

Every **push a new build to Cloudflare quadreal** must include `npm run sync:qr360-viewer` in the GitHub repo before build/deploy (the skill then mirrors to the Cloudflare folder) so online tours are not stuck on an old viewer.

Map topbar version (`v1.14.x`) is the **map app**. The badge inside a tour (`Map360-v1.2.x`) is the **embedded viewer** — different numbers by design.

## When the user ships a new viewer version

1. Confirm the new HTML exists in the Inspections source folder (QR360 badge).
2. Run from `QR-East_Industrial_Database`:

```powershell
npm run sync:qr360-viewer
```

3. That **replaces** older files in `qr360-viewer/`, overwrites `public/insp360/viewer.html`, and stamps **Map360-v…**.
4. Tell the user to hard-refresh BME / reopen the gate sphere — badge should read **Map360-v…**.

Do not hand-edit `public/insp360/viewer.html` — edit the Inspections source, then sync.
